"plan","bead_id":"bob-cli-rv.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-rv[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Datetime stamps on every task log entry[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every new Schedule, Rotten, Cancel, and Reopen Log entry, from [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]every bob-cli and plugin writer, carries one `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]stamp of the minute it was written, exactly as Work Log entries [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]already do. Older date-only entries stay valid and untouched, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]every reader, recall band, and display handles both forms.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]9[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_log_datetime_stamps.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/task_log_datetime_stamps.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-rv[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-rv/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-cli readers, recall, and snapshot accept stamps[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-readers[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-readers: add the shared Rust stamp formatter and parser. Teach `bob [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]logs` (parse, score, precision, cache) and the highlights note snapshot [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to read stamped entries in every log. Publish the canonical reader [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]grammar, and mark the JSON change with `!`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plugin Rotten and Schedule readers and recall bands accept [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]stamps[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]plugin-readers[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugin-readers: make the nav and ledger-tools Rotten Log parsers, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav Schedule Log parser, and both plugins' recall-age precision accept [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stamped and legacy entries. Displays show the time. Deploy both plugins [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]before any plugin writer stamps.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-cli Cancel Log writers stamp entries[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-cancel[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-readers[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-cancel: split the cancel engine's log stamp from `\\[cancelled::]`, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and stamp every Rust Cancel writer: relation cancel, merge, offer close,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gcal, and requirement drop. Regenerate the canonical shared fixtures [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with a `stamp` input.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-cli Schedule and Reopen Log writers stamp entries[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-schedule-reopen[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-readers, plugin-readers[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-schedule-reopen: stamp the capture `$<N>`, `bob task reroll`, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pull-forward Schedule entries and the gmail Reopen entry from one `now` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]per run, in the chosen layout. Mark the capture JSON change with `!`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Navigation hotkeys stamp Rotten and Schedule entries[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-rotten-schedule[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-readers, plugin-readers[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-rotten-schedule: add the generic plugin stamp formatter. Stamp every[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-navigation-hotkeys Rotten and Schedule writer and preview from one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit-time clock read per gesture, shared with that gesture's Work Log [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]entries.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Navigation hotkeys stamp Cancel entries[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-cancel[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-rotten-schedule, cli-cancel[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-cancel: split nav's cancel planners' stamp from `\\[cancelled::]`. Add[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]an optional `stamp` to the `cancel.planCancel` API and stamp every nav [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Cancel writer. Copy the regenerated task_cancel and task_split fixtures.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Cycler and Block ID Prompt stamp their entries; requirement [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]twins follow bob-cli[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cycler-bip[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-cancel, cli-cancel, cli-schedule-reopen[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cycler-bip: stamp task-status-cycler's unblock Schedule entry, its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]planCancel callers, and the cycler-owned requirement-writer twin, copied[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]byte for byte to nav. Stamp Block ID Prompt's pull-forward entry. Copy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the regenerated task_reqs, req_close, and offer_close fixtures.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Mac Capture re-syncs fixtures and pins minute recall ages[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]mac[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-readers, cli-cancel[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac: re-copy the regenerated req_close vectors, add tests that a minute [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Cancel `last_used` renders a minute age, and refresh the stale day-only [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]comments.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Decision record and Rotten Log glossary follow the stamped [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]grammar[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]memory[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cycler-bip[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory: apply the accepted memory decisions (the new decision record [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with its supersession marks, and the Rotten Log glossary grammar), then [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]regenerate AGENTS.md and the generated docs.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-rv","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-rv.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"bob-cli-rv.1"},"source_run_id":"run-09d146b6d83173a12bbd3431deb0f061","started_at":"2026-11-28T13:24:35.448530+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"1b0272faac61320314c47c4a13fe3e2fc97353bd68c99342af698cb004cce744","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rv.2/chat.md","size_bytes":4681},"commits":{"digest":"3694b455958e9e45b7938c41523a57a0ec9c7383bb4d6b4a18ed9fdc5ce6390b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rv.2/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"3942241a63c5de53df93bede886ed35a51f8b6a33d5883d819c898d7dd34f408","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rv.2/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":83},"meta":{"digest":"99122cb93c76abf267da9035c87eca6897b216f12b98c99924c407230ac62964","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rv.2/meta.json","size_bytes":669},"prompt